16. State priority

Preserve the established state-machine priorities.

Charge must never override higher-priority combat or airborne states.

A suitable ordering is:

hitstun
attack
jump / fall
land
block
charge
run
idle

This means:

* being hit immediately replaces Charge with Hurt/Hitstun
* starting BA1/BA2 interrupts Charge
* jumping interrupts Charge
* being airborne prevents Charge
* Block has priority if Block and Charge are both held
* Charge overrides normal Run/Idle presentation while actually active

Do not weaken BA1 or BA2 behavior.

